<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Madam Walker returns two weeks after starting losartan 50 mg, empagliflozin 10 mg and atorvastatin 20 mg. She has taken them each morning at home time, including on a four-day trip. Her home readings average 144/90, down from 152/96. The morning headaches have stopped. She has had no dizziness, cough, genital itching or muscle aches, and urinates slightly more in the first hours after the empagliflozin. She had a video session with the dietitian and has made a salt-free version of her seasoning blend. Her hepatitis B, hepatitis C and HIV tests were negative, and she has no hepatitis B immunity. The echocardiogram was done this morning. She leaves next week for three weeks of conventions. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Average 144/90 on losartan 50 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Diet</td><td>Dietitian session done; salt-free seasoning blend</td></tr><tr><td>Screening tests</td><td>Hepatitis B and C and HIV negative; no hepatitis B immunity</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

